	(text "Slicer: TLV3605 LVDS comparator (U20). IN+ = SDET, IN- = VTH. Left to right: inputs, comparator, LVDS pair out."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 50.8 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3a5185be-a5db-4248-b111-b3021f8e96c9")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A, nothing here is simulated or measured)\nPROPOSED  IN+ = SDET (AC-coupled detector output), IN- = VTH (threshold from Control). Output high when SDET > VTH.\nPROPOSED  VCCI = VCCO = 3V3. VCCI direct to 3V3; VCCO through R80 0R (option for a bead). Each pin has 100 nF 0402 + 1 uF 0603.\nVERIFIED  Supply range 2.4 V to 5.5 V; separate VCCI/VCCO; bypass 0.1 uF ceramic directly between VCCI/VCCO and VEE (SNOSDA2F p.19, 7.3 and 7.4.1 item 2).\nPROPOSED  SHDN (pin 7): R81 10k pull-up to 3V3; SHDN_N from Control, active low. VIH 1.5 V min, VIL 0.4 V max, 1.8 V logic compatible (SNOSDA2F p.8, EC table, and p.13 6.4).\n          Shutdown is not a guaranteed zero output (standing correction 11); the FPGA watchdog must catch a stuck output.\nVERIFIED  LE/HYS (pin 8): output latches when the pin is below 800 mV above VEE (p.14, 7.1.3; EC table VIL_LE 0.35 V max, VIH_LE 1.5 V min, p.8).\n          Floating = 0 mV hysteresis; resistor to VEE sets it: 150k = 30 mV, 56k = 60 mV (p.8 and p.15, 7.1.4).\nPROPOSED  R82 150k to GND = 30 mV hysteresis (R82 footprint also takes 56k for 60 mV). R83 0R, DNP: fit only if the FPGA is to force the latch.\nUNRESOLVED  Pin voltage of LE/HYS with R82 fitted is not given in the datasheet. If R83 is fitted the FPGA must drive low only (open drain) or tri-state; driving high may override the hysteresis setting.\nPROPOSED  OUT+ = LVDS_P, OUT- = LVDS_N, VOD 350 mV typ into 100 ohm. No termination on this board: the ECP5 has on-die 100 ohm termination (docs/research/ulx3s-lvds-input.md).\nPROPOSED  VEE (3, 5, 9, 11) and exposed pad (13) to GND. Datasheet gives no pad connection requirement beyond layout item 1 (solid ground plane); pad tied to GND by this schematic.\nPROPOSED  TP20 VTH, TP21 SDET (DNP: the probe adds load on SDET). Keep SDET and VTH traces short and matched; OUT+/OUT- matched length (p.19 layout items 3 and 6)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 50.8 175 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f81491b8-1d9d-4b69-be5d-917d7f31a66a")
	)
